  <div class="callout-box">
    <strong>Key Baseline Finding:</strong> While packaged food wrappers represented 58.7% of all individual plastic units logged (27 units), <strong>PET water bottles accounted for an overwhelming 79.2% of total plastic weight (342.0 g)</strong>. Therefore, eliminating packaged water bottles through reusable alternatives is the single highest-leverage intervention for campus plastic reduction.
  </div>

  <h2>1.4 Week 1 Baseline vs. Week 2 "Daily Carry Kit" Challenge Comparison</h2>
  <p>
    During Week 2, our team deployed the student-designed <strong>"Daily Carry Kit"</strong> (stainless steel bottle, cloth jhola, and reusable cutlery). A direct empirical comparison reveals the transformative potential of simple habit swaps:
  </p>

