  <div class="callout-box-blue">
    <strong>UPI Payment Correlation Analysis:</strong> During Week 2, despite higher transaction frequency (32 micro-payments vs 18 in Week 1 due to academic exam week confectionery purchases), our plastic mass dropped from 432.0g to 263.5g. The plastic density per payment fell from 2.6 items to 1.4 items, proving that carrying a steel water bottle successfully decoupled daily student transactions from heavy plastic mass generation.
  </div>

  <h2>1.5 Institutional Extrapolation Across Campus</h2>
  <p>
    Extrapolating these empirical results across a representative model campus of <strong>500 residential students</strong> over an academic calendar of <strong>40 active semester weeks</strong> underscores the monumental scale of institutional plastic pollution:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Per Student Weekly Generation:</strong> 144.0 grams / week (432.0g &divide; 3 students).</li>
    <li><strong>Per Student Annual Generation:</strong> 5.76 kg of single-use plastic per student / academic year.</li>
    <li><strong>Campus-Wide 500-Student Annual Plastic Footprint:</strong> <strong>2,880 kg (2.88 Metric Tonnes)</strong> of single-use plastic per year.</li>
    <li><strong>PET Bottle Equivalent:</strong> 126,600 single-use bottles discarded annually on campus grounds.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>1.6 The "Daily Carry Kit" Action Simulator &amp; Financial Payback</h2>
  <p>
    Recognizing that college students operate on limited monthly pocket money, our intervention framework focuses on practical, low-cost habit swaps with rapid financial payback periods:
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Kit &amp; Culprit Item</th>
        <th>Single-Use Habit</th>
        <th>Green Reusable Alternative</th>
        <th>Capital Cost &amp; Payback</th>
        <th style="text-align: right;">Annual Plastic Saved</th>
        <th style="text-align: right;">Annual Student Savings</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Part A: Backpack Kit</strong><br/><span class="kpi-sub">Always Carried</span></td>
        <td>Buying 20 Kinley/Bisleri PET bottles weekly at canteen</td>
        <td><strong>Reusable Stainless Steel Bottle (1 Litre)</strong> refilled at certified campus RO stations</td>
        <td>Cost: ₹250–400<br/><strong>Breaks even after 13–20 refills</strong></td>
        <td style="text-align: right; font-weight: bold; color: #1e3a2f;">3.60 kg / student</td>
