  <h2>2.5 Campus Recycled Water Allocation &amp; Financial Payback</h2>
  <p>
    Accounting for ~6% natural evapotranspiration loss in the wetland bed, the 100-student hostel system yields <strong>4,230 Litres / day (94% recovery yield)</strong> of clean non-potable water, distributed as follows:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Campus Botanical Gardens &amp; Lawn Irrigation (45%):</strong> 1,904 L/day distributed through subsurface drip lines.</li>
    <li><strong>Dual-Plumbing Toilet &amp; Urinal Flushing (35%):</strong> 1,481 L/day pumped to overhead dedicated header tanks.</li>
    <li><strong>HVAC Cooling Tower Makeup &amp; Dust Suppression (20%):</strong> 846 L/day utilized in academic block utilities.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="callout-box-amber">
    <strong>Financial Payback:</strong> Producing 4,230 L/day saves <strong>1,544,000 Litres (1,544 kL) of municipal/tanker freshwater annually</strong>. At current commercial water tanker tariffs of ₹45 per 1,000 Litres (kL), this delivers <strong>₹69,480 in annual direct operational savings</strong>, amortizing the passive wetland civil construction cost in under 3.5 years.
  </div>

